    2	{"role":"user","content":"Research the following information about United States Secretaries of Homeland Security:\n\n1. List all individuals who formally held the position of United States Secretary of Homeland Security prior to April 2019, excluding those who held the position in an acting capacity.\n\n2. For each of these individuals, find the university where they earned their bachelor's degree.\n\n3. Identify which university is the westernmost and which is the easternmost based on the cities where they are located.\n\n4. Return the names of the cities where these universities are located, with the westernmost city listed first, as a comma-separated list.\n\nPlease be thorough and verify the information. The position of Secretary of Homeland Security was created in 2003. Prior to April 2019, the formal (non-acting) secretaries would be:\n- Tom Ridge (first Secretary, 2003-2005)\n- Michael Chertoff (2005-2009)\n- Janet Napolitano (2009-2013)\n- Jeh Johnson (2013-2017)\n- John F. Kelly (2017-2017)\n- Kirstjen Nielsen (2017-2019)\n\nBut I need you to verify this list and find their bachelor's degree universities. Note that some may have served as acting secretaries before becoming formal secretaries - exclude those who only held acting positions.\n\nSearch the web for each person's educational background to find where they got their bachelor's degrees. Then determine the cities and their locations (longitude) to find westernmost and easternmost."}
